# Overview

This educational REST API demonstrates how to build a complete CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) application using Node.js and Express.js. The code is organized into separate modules following the separation of concerns principle: data storage, error handling, middleware, and routing are each isolated in their own files. This structure mirrors real-world applications where different responsibilities are managed by distinct components.

The API uses an in-memory array for simplicity (no database setup required), but includes detailed comments explaining when you would transition to a persistent database like MongoDB or PostgreSQL. Every function includes JSDoc documentation, and the error handling system demonstrates custom error classes with proper HTTP status codes. The filtering system on GET /books shows how to handle query parameters safely.

